# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository.
#
# Windows checkout, Linux runtime. Without this, git stores whatever the
# working tree had, and a CRLF blob reaching Railway breaks things that a
# Windows editor never shows you: a heredoc terminator with a trailing \r
# never matches, and a shebang line becomes "/usr/bin/env node\r".
#
# eol=lf forces LF in the WORKING TREE too, not just in the blob. That is
# deliberate — test/*.js compare multi-line strings, and a harness that passes
# on Linux and fails on Windows because of an invisible \r costs an afternoon
# to find.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
*.pptx binary
*.ico  binary
